1
00:00:05,067 --> 00:00:12,100
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,867 --> 00:00:32,933
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,333 --> 00:00:35,333
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:41,367
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,167
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:45,467
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,467 --> 00:00:46,600
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,433
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,833 --> 00:00:53,900
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,600
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,300
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,467
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,167
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:06,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,433 --> 00:01:09,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:11,933
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,933 --> 00:01:13,333
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:14,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:22,933
<i> For now, prepare
to transfer Victor Zafra.</i>

21
00:01:22,933 --> 00:01:25,300
<i>I don't trust the NCIA.
I'm counting on you.</i>

22
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:27,400
<i>You have to go
to the NCIA right now.</i>

23
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,967
<i> - What are you waiting for?
- Let's go!</i>

24
00:01:28,967 --> 00:01:31,433
Victor's going to be transferred
<i> to maximum security today.</i>

25
00:01:31,433 --> 00:01:33,400
<i> Signal Victor when it's time.</i>

26
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:34,833
<i> Here is the court order.</i>

27
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:38,100
<i>To make it clear that
your transfer process is legal.</i>

28
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:39,400
<i> This is our best chance.</i>

29
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:43,167
We're going to have a hard time
<i> finding another chance.</i>

30
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,567
<i> I'll bring your son home.</i>

31
00:01:44,567 --> 00:01:45,567
<i> Love!</i>

32
00:01:45,567 --> 00:01:48,000
<i>You're Gloria!
I'm your husband Gabo!</i>

33
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,300
<i> Are you really my husband?</i>

34
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:51,633
<i>You didn't tell us about that!
Gabo, what's with you?!</i>

35
00:01:51,633 --> 00:01:53,433
<i> You think you can fool me?</i>

36
00:01:53,433 --> 00:01:57,000
<i>I'll find out your connection
to Zafra and Mr. Chan.</i>

37
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,667
<i> She can't remember a thing.
She's got amnesia.</i>

38
00:01:58,667 --> 00:01:59,700
<i> So we need to pretend.</i>

39
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:01,000
<i>No one else should know
about this.</i>

40
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,500
Only we know who she really is.

41
00:02:05,533 --> 00:02:06,900
[WOMAN] Poor guy.

42
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:09,700
He's so kind that people
take advantage of him.

43
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,033
Even when he tries to avoid it,

44
00:02:11,033 --> 00:02:13,933
bad luck just keeps chasing him.

45
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:17,067
- I don't know why he's...
- [MAN] Where is the...

46
00:02:17,067 --> 00:02:24,000
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,500
[SAM]<i> I've been in the service
</i> for a long time,

48
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,867
<i>but I've never been
to a place like this.</i>

49
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:29,700
<i> Chances are,</i>

50
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:32,267
<i>no cop has ever dared
to set foot here</i>

51
00:02:32,667 --> 00:02:36,267
<i>because the people
are evil to the core.</i>

52
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:45,267
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

53
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:53,533
Victor Zafra is
a high-risk detainee,

54
00:02:53,533 --> 00:02:57,000
so let's assume the worst
during his trasfer.

55
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,433
Maintain communication,

56
00:02:58,433 --> 00:03:04,367
and nobody moves unless
Sebastian gives the word.

57
00:03:04,367 --> 00:03:05,333
Understand?

58
00:03:05,333 --> 00:03:06,333
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

59
00:03:06,333 --> 00:03:07,433
[DOORS OPEN]

60
00:03:07,433 --> 00:03:08,900
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

61
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:10,267
[UMALI] Sir Delgado.

62
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:11,733
Good day to you.

63
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,167
[DELGADO]
What are you doing here?

64
00:03:13,167 --> 00:03:15,967
[UMALI] General Jacinto called
our station.

65
00:03:15,967 --> 00:03:20,300
He said you're transferring a
detainee to maximum security.

66
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,533
[DELGADO]
This is an NCIA operation.

67
00:03:22,567 --> 00:03:24,167
It's none of your business.

68
00:03:24,167 --> 00:03:25,133
[UMALI CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

69
00:03:25,133 --> 00:03:28,233
Sir, we're not trying
to interfere.

70
00:03:28,233 --> 00:03:30,367
We're just here
to reinforce security.

71
00:03:30,367 --> 00:03:32,767
[DELGADO]
We have enough men to do that.

72
00:03:33,233 --> 00:03:36,300
[UMALI] General Jacinto called
the station himself.

73
00:03:37,267 --> 00:03:39,167
Who am I supposed to follow
between the two of you?

74
00:03:39,167 --> 00:03:41,300
[DELGADO] I don't care
if he's a general.

75
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:44,333
General Jacinto doesn't
control the NCIA!

76
00:03:44,967 --> 00:03:46,500
[SEBASTIAN] We don't need you.

77
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:47,900
You'll only cause trouble.

78
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:49,767
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

79
00:03:49,767 --> 00:03:51,200
Let me guess.

80
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:54,633
General Jacinto called us

81
00:03:54,667 --> 00:03:56,933
because he doubts what
your men can actually handle.

82
00:03:57,933 --> 00:04:00,500
[DELGADO]
I didn't sign any papers

83
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,267
saying we'd request
extra manpower from the NLEA.

84
00:04:02,267 --> 00:04:03,367
You can all leave now.

85
00:04:03,933 --> 00:04:04,933
[SNICKERS]

86
00:04:05,767 --> 00:04:06,800
Hear that?

87
00:04:08,333 --> 00:04:10,067
They don't need our help.

88
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:12,767
[SCOFFS]

89
00:04:12,767 --> 00:04:14,267
You're the expert, huh?

90
00:04:14,967 --> 00:04:16,000
Let's go.

91
00:04:21,967 --> 00:04:23,067
[MUSIC ENDS]

92
00:04:23,067 --> 00:04:26,700
- [HEAVY FOOTSTEPS]
- [CUP CLINKING]

93
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:27,700
Ma.

94
00:04:28,267 --> 00:04:29,767
I'll head back
to the police station.

95
00:04:30,533 --> 00:04:31,533
[SOFTLY] Okay.

96
00:04:33,033 --> 00:04:34,133
[MAX SIGHS]

97
00:04:34,933 --> 00:04:36,033
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

98
00:04:36,033 --> 00:04:37,700
Why don't you get some rest?

99
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:39,833
How can I rest?

100
00:04:40,167 --> 00:04:42,133
I'm worried about my daughter.

101
00:04:42,133 --> 00:04:43,833
I'm worried too, Ma.

102
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,800
But worrying
won't do us any good.

103
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:50,433
We both know that
Sam is a strong woman.

104
00:04:50,433 --> 00:04:52,200
She's even stronger than I am.

105
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,200
So, please.

106
00:04:54,167 --> 00:04:55,567
Stop worrying,

107
00:04:55,567 --> 00:04:57,800
because Sam will be
safely returned to us.

108
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:00,200
That's easy for you to say

109
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,867
because you have
grown desensitized

110
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:04,500
to people going missing
and being kidnapped.

111
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:07,167
But I'm just an ordinary mom...

112
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:09,467
...who's worried
about her daughter.

113
00:05:09,467 --> 00:05:11,200
[MAX] I understand, Ma.

114
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:14,733
I'm also worried
about my sister.

115
00:05:15,567 --> 00:05:17,100
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

116
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:19,167
I actually feel guilty,
Ma, because...

117
00:05:20,167 --> 00:05:23,500
we haven't been on good terms
these past few days.

118
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,733
We will not lose her, Ma, okay?

119
00:05:27,733 --> 00:05:29,067
I promise you that.

120
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:30,567
I will find her.

121
00:05:30,567 --> 00:05:32,333
I'm still hoping that...

122
00:05:32,333 --> 00:05:35,567
...someday, somehow, Dad
will be able to forgive Sam.

123
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:39,433
Then the four of us can be
a happy family. Okay?

124
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:47,033
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

125
00:05:54,267 --> 00:05:55,433
I'll find her, okay?

126
00:05:56,033 --> 00:05:57,067
[ISOBEL WHISPERS] Alright.

127
00:06:02,933 --> 00:06:04,167
[HEAVY FOOTSTEPS]

128
00:06:04,167 --> 00:06:11,100
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

129
00:06:13,367 --> 00:06:14,467
[DELGADO] Tiger.

130
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,567
Unless you talk,

131
00:06:18,567 --> 00:06:20,700
you'll waste away in prison.

132
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,767
[CHUCKLING]

133
00:06:26,533 --> 00:06:28,167
What's so funny?

134
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,933
I'm just happy
about where I'm going.

135
00:06:30,933 --> 00:06:33,133
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

136
00:06:33,133 --> 00:06:34,167
[DELGADO] Team.

137
00:06:34,867 --> 00:06:36,367
Be extra vigilant.

138
00:06:36,367 --> 00:06:38,300
Stay sharp
for any breakout attempt.

139
00:06:39,633 --> 00:06:41,167
I'm counting on all of you.

140
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,333
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

141
00:06:42,333 --> 00:06:43,600
- Now, move.
- [SEBASTIAN] Come on.

142
00:06:51,467 --> 00:06:52,500
- Rudy.
- Hmm?

143
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:54,267
[ELTON] Is she Gabo's wife?

144
00:06:54,267 --> 00:06:55,733
Geez, she's beautiful.

145
00:06:55,733 --> 00:06:56,867
Where did he meet her?

146
00:06:56,867 --> 00:06:58,467
[RUDY] We don't know.

147
00:06:58,467 --> 00:06:59,667
We were just as surprised.

148
00:06:59,667 --> 00:07:02,500
[DANTE] He didn't even tell us
he got married already.

149
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:04,900
- He did. Remember?
- Did he?

150
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:06,100
Her skin's shining.

151
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:08,000
She doesn't fit here,
she's too pretty!

152
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,600
Can you stop looking at her?
Leave them alone!

153
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:13,733
Does she have an aunt?
She's beautiful!

154
00:07:13,733 --> 00:07:15,633
- [RUDY] Oh, yeah, she does.
- Really?

155
00:07:15,667 --> 00:07:16,833
Yeah, she has a grandma.

156
00:07:16,833 --> 00:07:18,633
She's 102 years old.
Just clean her up.

157
00:07:18,633 --> 00:07:21,233
- [DANTE CHUCKLING]
- [ELTON] You're too much.

158
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:25,567
- Hey, who's that?
- Who's gonna finish this?

159
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:28,767
Ah, she's Gloria, Miss Diday.
She's Gabo's wife.

160
00:07:28,767 --> 00:07:30,633
- Gabo's wife?! Is that true?!
- Yes!

161
00:07:30,633 --> 00:07:32,367
- Yes!
- See, there's his wife.

162
00:07:32,367 --> 00:07:35,267
[DIDAY] Gabo hasn't told me
about her.

163
00:07:35,267 --> 00:07:36,400
I should go ask.

164
00:07:37,567 --> 00:07:39,100
Is it necessary
that she knows about her?

165
00:07:39,933 --> 00:07:42,767
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

166
00:07:42,767 --> 00:07:44,433
Are you Gabo's wife?

167
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:47,800
Uh...

168
00:07:49,067 --> 00:07:51,000
- Yes.
- My name is Diday.

169
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,100
What's your name?

170
00:07:52,833 --> 00:07:59,567
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

171
00:07:59,567 --> 00:08:03,933
Your name is Gloria!
That's what they said.

172
00:08:03,933 --> 00:08:05,000
Ah. [CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

173
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:08,867
You're beautiful!
And your skin seems smooth!

174
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:13,300
How did you put up with Gabo?
How did he bring you here?

175
00:08:14,233 --> 00:08:18,867
Oh, no. I'm sorry.
I don't remember anything.

176
00:08:18,867 --> 00:08:21,167
Ma, stop asking questions!

177
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:23,133
Let's go,
you're embarrassing us.

178
00:08:23,133 --> 00:08:25,167
What's so embarrassing?
Just wait for a second!

179
00:08:25,167 --> 00:08:28,733
We've never had anyone
so pretty in our community.

180
00:08:28,733 --> 00:08:31,900
You know what?
Gabo's handsomeness...

181
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:33,933
...is on the same level
as Gloria's beauty.

182
00:08:33,933 --> 00:08:35,100
- Hey!
- You're right.

183
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:37,100
Gabo is very lucky.

184
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:39,400
Especially if they do
end up together!

185
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:41,133
Wow, where's your loyalty?

186
00:08:41,133 --> 00:08:42,833
- Why don't you stop drinking?
- Nah.

187
00:08:42,833 --> 00:08:45,700
- You're our boss. Boss, boss.
- I don't think that'll happen.

188
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:48,333
How will they end up together
when she's an NCIA agent?

189
00:08:49,367 --> 00:08:51,233
I can assure you of one thing.

190
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:56,200
Never! And I mean never
will Gloria ever like Gabo!

191
00:08:56,233 --> 00:08:58,700
Exactly! This is why I like you.

192
00:08:58,700 --> 00:09:00,333
- That's what friends are for.
- [DABOY] Besides,

193
00:09:00,333 --> 00:09:02,200
if Gloria's memory comes back,

194
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:05,133
I'm sure Gabo will end up
in jail.

195
00:09:05,133 --> 00:09:06,700
- That, too.
- Oh, yeah.

196
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:18,067
[MUSIC TURNS SWEET]

197
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,833
They do everything
just to harass all of us here!

198
00:09:23,833 --> 00:09:25,367
And I don't understand

199
00:09:25,367 --> 00:09:27,000
- how my nephew's so kind,
- Auntie!

200
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,333
- but they--
- Where's Gloria?

201
00:09:28,367 --> 00:09:29,633
She's here!

202
00:09:30,567 --> 00:09:31,567
Oh.

203
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:33,367
- She was just here.
- [BOWL THUDS]

204
00:09:33,367 --> 00:09:35,067
I was talking to her.
She was even answering back!

205
00:09:35,067 --> 00:09:36,300
- Gloria!
- Hey!

206
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:37,833
- [DOOR CREAKS]
- Gloria?

207
00:09:37,833 --> 00:09:38,767
Miss Diday.

208
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:41,333
- Ah.
- [SAM CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

209
00:09:41,333 --> 00:09:44,433
Miss Diday,
this is my wife Gloria.

210
00:09:44,433 --> 00:09:47,333
So you're married now, Gabo.
I wish you had told us.

211
00:09:47,333 --> 00:09:49,367
- She's pretty!
- Yes.

212
00:09:49,367 --> 00:09:54,567
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

213
00:09:54,567 --> 00:09:56,467
This was just sudden,
Miss Diday.

214
00:09:57,033 --> 00:10:00,367
I didn't know
she was coming home last night.

215
00:10:00,367 --> 00:10:01,833
I was surprised, too.

216
00:10:01,867 --> 00:10:04,067
[DIDAY] Why doesn't she seem
to be in the right mind

217
00:10:04,067 --> 00:10:05,600
when I'm asking her things?

218
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,267
[MAMENG] Um, Diday.

219
00:10:07,267 --> 00:10:09,467
Don't ask the kid
too many questions.

220
00:10:09,467 --> 00:10:11,533
She's still a bit confused.

221
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:13,400
Uh, Miss Diday...

222
00:10:14,567 --> 00:10:16,767
She just arrived last night.

223
00:10:16,767 --> 00:10:19,500
She's so hardworking
that she did laundry last night,

224
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:21,300
and even climbed up the roof.

225
00:10:21,833 --> 00:10:23,600
She hung the clothes there,
but she fell!

226
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:25,300
She hit her head.

227
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:27,933
Right now,
she doesn't remember anything.

228
00:10:27,933 --> 00:10:31,667
We think she has a-amnesia.

229
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:36,967
- She lost her memories.
- [DIDAY] Gabo, you're lucky.

230
00:10:37,833 --> 00:10:39,333
- She's pretty.
- [GABO CHUCKLES]

231
00:10:39,333 --> 00:10:42,133
Your kids will be pretty
and fair-skinned!

232
00:10:42,133 --> 00:10:43,500
- [GABO CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]
- Right?

233
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:44,867
O-Of course.

234
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:49,467
Uh, since when did I get here?

235
00:10:49,467 --> 00:10:50,500
Uh...

236
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:53,633
Honey. Uh...

237
00:10:53,633 --> 00:10:54,900
You just arrived last night.

238
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:57,267
I was actually surprised
about your coming here.

239
00:10:57,267 --> 00:10:58,567
I didn't know you got released.

240
00:10:58,567 --> 00:11:05,667
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

241
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,267
I got released?

242
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:10,900
Uh, yes!

243
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:13,233
You've been in prison
for a long time.

244
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:16,567
I mean, you even got
a life sentence.

245
00:11:17,667 --> 00:11:19,233
Why? What were the charges
against me?

246
00:11:20,933 --> 00:11:23,100
Um...

247
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:26,033
Uh, f-fraud!

248
00:11:27,333 --> 00:11:28,733
You scammed people,

249
00:11:28,733 --> 00:11:31,533
and didn't you kill those
who were collecting from you?

250
00:11:31,533 --> 00:11:34,200
Oh my! Fraud? Murder?!

251
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:35,533
You got a life sentence!

252
00:11:36,167 --> 00:11:42,500
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

253
00:11:42,533 --> 00:11:44,333
[DIDAY]
Your charges are extreme!

254
00:11:44,333 --> 00:11:47,400
I went to prison
because of homicide!

255
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:49,133
What group were you with inside?

256
00:11:50,767 --> 00:11:54,667
Oh, I'm so sorry.
I don't remember anything.

257
00:11:54,667 --> 00:11:58,400
My group inside was Bruha.

258
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,200
[SMACKS ARM]

259
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,667
This is the tough woman.

260
00:12:02,933 --> 00:12:09,900
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

261
00:12:11,367 --> 00:12:13,667
She doesn't have tattoos!
She's clean!

262
00:12:13,667 --> 00:12:18,067
Well, Miss Diday,
she's elegant in prison.

263
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:20,400
No one gets close to her.
No one survives.

264
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:21,667
She kills them all.

265
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:24,567
Oh, Gabo,
you got the jackpot!

266
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:28,967
- Tekla!
- Oh?

267
00:12:28,967 --> 00:12:31,900
You're nothing against Gloria!
She's very pretty!

268
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:33,833
But you, you're outdated!

269
00:12:33,833 --> 00:12:37,000
- Ohh!
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

270
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,667
You'll have
to excuse Miss Diday.

271
00:12:38,667 --> 00:12:39,833
That's just how she is.

272
00:12:39,833 --> 00:12:42,133
When she drinks, she's even
braver and more chatty.

273
00:12:42,133 --> 00:12:44,767
[MAMENG] Dear, I'm sorry.

274
00:12:44,767 --> 00:12:47,667
This is how we are over here.

275
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:49,300
Uh...

276
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:52,267
Is it true?
Did I go to prison?

277
00:12:53,567 --> 00:12:56,767
Uh, yeah! It's true!

278
00:12:56,767 --> 00:12:59,000
I was surprised
you came home last night.

279
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,167
I wasn't expecting it.

280
00:13:01,333 --> 00:13:05,567
I thought
you'll be in prison forever.

281
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:09,400
That's why
when we got married...

282
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,900
I wasn't hoping
that we'd meet outside.

283
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:18,200
But, like I promised you...

284
00:13:19,267 --> 00:13:21,300
I waited for you
no matter what.

285
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:27,200
I promised that
once you were free,

286
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,933
and we were finally together...

287
00:13:29,967 --> 00:13:31,800
I'll love you
and take care of you.

288
00:13:32,467 --> 00:13:34,067
So now that we're together...

289
00:13:35,433 --> 00:13:40,167
I promise I'd care for you
and love you endlessly.

290
00:13:42,533 --> 00:13:43,600
Gloria...

291
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:46,700
I love you so much.

292
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:49,333
You're my beloved.

293
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:58,233
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

294
00:14:00,467 --> 00:14:01,533
[SAM] This jerk.

295
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,567
<i>You're taking advantage
of me, huh?</i>

296
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:06,500
<i>You're making the most
out of this.</i>

297
00:14:10,267 --> 00:14:14,833
<i>Once I finish my mission,
you better prepare yourself!</i>

298
00:14:14,833 --> 00:14:16,233
<i> I'll get back at you.</i>

299
00:14:16,233 --> 00:14:23,200
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

300
00:14:29,067 --> 00:14:32,233
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

301
00:14:32,233 --> 00:14:37,933
[POLICE SIREN WAILING]

302
00:14:37,933 --> 00:14:40,433
[CAR DOORS OPEN]

303
00:14:40,433 --> 00:14:41,833
[CAR DOORS CLOSE]

304
00:14:41,833 --> 00:14:42,800
Men!

305
00:14:43,567 --> 00:14:45,033
- You know what to do.
- Yes, ma'am!

306
00:14:45,033 --> 00:14:46,667
Go. Estrella, come with me.

307
00:14:46,667 --> 00:14:47,600
Let's go.

308
00:14:49,133 --> 00:14:50,800
[DOGS BARKING IN DISTANCE]

309
00:14:52,467 --> 00:14:54,533
- Good day.
- Good day, ma'am.

310
00:14:54,533 --> 00:14:55,833
Have you seen this woman?

311
00:14:55,833 --> 00:14:57,900
No, I didn't.
You can try asking over there.

312
00:14:58,733 --> 00:15:00,067
Come on, Estrella. Thank you.

313
00:15:00,067 --> 00:15:01,033
Okay.

314
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:06,567
Good day.
Have you seen this woman?

315
00:15:07,467 --> 00:15:10,067
Excuse me, ma'am. Good day.
Have you seen this woman?

316
00:15:10,067 --> 00:15:11,667
No, I'm sorry.

317
00:15:11,667 --> 00:15:13,767
- I'd like to buy some, please.
- Good day.

318
00:15:13,767 --> 00:15:14,867
Have you seen this woman?

319
00:15:14,867 --> 00:15:16,567
No. I'm sorry.

320
00:15:16,567 --> 00:15:18,000
[ESTRELLA] Maybe you guys
have seen this woman?

321
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,500
- [WOMAN] No, I didn't.
- Excuse me. Good day, sir.

322
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:22,400
- Yes, ma'am?
- Have you seen this woman?

323
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:23,800
[MAN] I'm sorry, I didn't.

324
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:25,100
How about you, sir?
Take a good look at it.

325
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,167
[MAN] No, I didn't.

326
00:15:27,067 --> 00:15:31,433
Neighbors! They found a corpse
by the junkyard!

327
00:15:31,433 --> 00:15:33,400
Let's go! Come with me!

328
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:34,400
Come on!

329
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:35,900
[MUSIC TURNS ROUSING]

330
00:15:35,933 --> 00:15:37,167
Where?

331
00:15:37,167 --> 00:15:39,867
- Oh, I'm sorry. Don't worry.
- [QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

332
00:15:39,867 --> 00:15:42,133
We'll change it later
so it heals fast.

333
00:15:44,467 --> 00:15:46,433
Gloria, come.

334
00:15:46,433 --> 00:15:47,433
Let's sit over there.

335
00:15:48,533 --> 00:15:50,933
Auntie, Gloria and I
will just sit there.

336
00:15:50,933 --> 00:15:53,367
What? They'll join us here?
I paid for the drinks.

337
00:15:53,367 --> 00:15:56,433
I won't pay for hers! Buy her
a drink if you want her here!

338
00:15:57,733 --> 00:15:58,700
Careful.

339
00:15:59,433 --> 00:16:01,067
Gabo! Bottoms up!

340
00:16:01,067 --> 00:16:03,367
Tekla bought us drinks
because she's jealous--

341
00:16:03,367 --> 00:16:05,033
- Hmm?!
- I mean on her phone.

342
00:16:05,033 --> 00:16:07,400
She's glued to her phone.

343
00:16:08,867 --> 00:16:10,067
- Careful.
- [TEKLA] Don't give her any!

344
00:16:10,067 --> 00:16:11,467
I paid for that!

345
00:16:11,467 --> 00:16:13,400
These are my friends.
Please excuse them.

346
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:14,567
They can get annoying.

347
00:16:14,567 --> 00:16:16,167
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

348
00:16:17,467 --> 00:16:19,967
Gabo, your wife is beautiful.

349
00:16:19,967 --> 00:16:22,167
You surely hit the jackpot.

350
00:16:22,167 --> 00:16:23,233
Of course.

351
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:27,833
Maybe she has a sister
you could introduce us to.

352
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:31,300
Stop fooling around. Shut it.

353
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,600
Dream on.
Besides, she's one of a kind.

354
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:35,300
One wrong move
and a bullet hits you.

355
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,967
Uh... bullet? Why a bullet?

356
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:41,700
[CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]

357
00:16:41,733 --> 00:16:43,133
You just got out of jail, right?

358
00:16:43,133 --> 00:16:45,833
That means
you're tough and feisty.

359
00:16:45,833 --> 00:16:47,933
That's why
she can't easily be fooled.

360
00:16:47,933 --> 00:16:49,367
- Yes.
- She'll fight

361
00:16:49,367 --> 00:16:50,733
and won't back down.

362
00:16:50,733 --> 00:16:53,433
Only one person can fight her.

363
00:16:53,433 --> 00:16:54,433
Who?

364
00:16:54,433 --> 00:16:56,233
Who else? Tekla, for sure.

365
00:16:56,233 --> 00:16:58,033
- She's madly jealous.
- [GUYS CHUCKLE]

366
00:16:58,033 --> 00:16:59,500
Shh! Shut it, man!

367
00:17:00,367 --> 00:17:02,933
- [DABOY] It's true.
- Why would she be jealous?

368
00:17:02,933 --> 00:17:04,367
Tekla.

369
00:17:04,367 --> 00:17:05,933
Gloria is asking.

370
00:17:05,933 --> 00:17:07,433
Why are you jealous?

371
00:17:07,433 --> 00:17:09,367
Why am I jealous? [SCOFFS]

372
00:17:09,367 --> 00:17:11,033
She's really asking
why I'm jealous?

373
00:17:11,033 --> 00:17:13,433
Why wouldn't I be?

374
00:17:13,433 --> 00:17:15,333
Gabo is mine!
Then you came and--

375
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:19,667
That's enough!
You're getting too naughty!

376
00:17:19,667 --> 00:17:21,600
Why?! It's true!

377
00:17:21,600 --> 00:17:23,067
I'm obviously prettier than her.

378
00:17:23,067 --> 00:17:24,667
Look! And hey,

379
00:17:24,667 --> 00:17:26,700
I'm sexier than you, girl.

380
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:28,800
You have fair skin
and you're tall, but that's it.

381
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:30,033
We're not scared of you.

382
00:17:30,033 --> 00:17:31,700
- You are not special.
- [BONG SHUSHES]

383
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:33,800
Uh...

384
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:36,900
Tekla, that's enough.

385
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:37,900
Why?

386
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:40,400
Uh, I think I'll go
and get some rest.

387
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,333
My wounds are starting to hurt.

388
00:17:42,333 --> 00:17:44,967
Does it? Poor thing.

389
00:17:49,033 --> 00:17:50,100
Love.

390
00:17:52,133 --> 00:17:54,133
I'll get back inside the house.

391
00:17:54,133 --> 00:17:55,833
My wounds are starting to hurt.

392
00:17:58,333 --> 00:17:59,367
Okay, I'll go with you.

393
00:17:59,367 --> 00:18:01,133
She's really getting
on my nerves.

394
00:18:01,133 --> 00:18:03,467
No, it's okay.
Stay with your friends.

395
00:18:03,467 --> 00:18:04,633
I'm fine.

396
00:18:04,633 --> 00:18:05,700
Ouch! Ouch!

397
00:18:07,833 --> 00:18:09,100
I'll get going, guys.

398
00:18:11,133 --> 00:18:14,533
[SAM]<i> Does she really think
</i> I like that guy?

399
00:18:15,533 --> 00:18:16,900
<i> Hell no! He looks scruffy!</i>

400
00:18:17,533 --> 00:18:19,100
<i> He looks like
he hasn't showered for days.</i>

401
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:21,533
<i> He looks like he stinks, too.</i>

402
00:18:21,567 --> 00:18:23,867
<i> You can have him all you want.</i>

403
00:18:23,867 --> 00:18:30,833
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

404
00:18:30,833 --> 00:18:33,867
What is she looking at?
Oh, she's trying to piss me off.

405
00:18:35,933 --> 00:18:37,067
She was looking at Gabo.

406
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:39,600
Tekla, sit down.

407
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:42,400
It's her fault, Gabo!

408
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:43,600
We've talked about this,
remember?

409
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:44,767
Didn't you get it?

410
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,067
You know her situation
and why she got here.

411
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:51,300
But I can't stand her, Gabo!

412
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:53,800
I've liked you since
we were kids, you know that!

413
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,900
And that fair-skinned lady
will just come into the picture?

414
00:18:55,933 --> 00:18:58,133
And she'll just take you
away from me that easily?!

415
00:18:58,133 --> 00:19:00,067
I can't let that happen.
I really can't.

416
00:19:00,067 --> 00:19:01,167
- Tekla.
- Sorry.

417
00:19:01,167 --> 00:19:02,200
Stop it.

418
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:04,733
We're doing this to protect her.

419
00:19:05,467 --> 00:19:07,133
Don't get any ideas
in your head.

420
00:19:07,133 --> 00:19:09,433
Tekla, don't make this hard.

421
00:19:09,433 --> 00:19:10,833
Don't you get
the weight of this?

422
00:19:10,833 --> 00:19:12,833
It's not that I don't get it!

423
00:19:12,833 --> 00:19:14,833
I just can't accept it!

424
00:19:14,833 --> 00:19:15,833
Tekla.

425
00:19:15,833 --> 00:19:16,933
[TEKLA EXHALES]

426
00:19:16,933 --> 00:19:18,633
Grow up, will you?

427
00:19:18,633 --> 00:19:19,600
[TEKLA HUFFS]

428
00:19:20,967 --> 00:19:23,700
Listen, she's in danger.

429
00:19:24,433 --> 00:19:27,800
No strangers can enter Paradise,
got it?

430
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:31,000
We need to keep our eyes
on every alley.

431
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Do you understand?

432
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,500
- Yes, Gabo.
- Yes, Gabo.

433
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:36,800
Don't worry. We'll assign men
to guard the streets.

434
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:39,433
We'll make sure
no outsiders come in here.

435
00:19:39,433 --> 00:19:41,600
If they attempt to,
we'll know right away.

436
00:19:42,333 --> 00:19:43,400
You got this, alright?

437
00:19:44,233 --> 00:19:45,533
I really need your help.

438
00:19:46,133 --> 00:19:48,100
Tekla, I'm counting on you.

439
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:52,600
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

440
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:55,100
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

441
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:56,200
Oh, that's a dead body for sure.

442
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:01,667
How many days has it been there?

443
00:20:02,533 --> 00:20:03,900
[MAN]
We might get dragged into this.

444
00:20:04,467 --> 00:20:07,733
[ESTRELLA] Please step back!
Step back!

445
00:20:07,733 --> 00:20:12,867
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

446
00:20:15,767 --> 00:20:17,067
Those goddamn
NCIA agents.

447
00:20:17,067 --> 00:20:18,967
Who do they think
they are? [SCOFFS]

448
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:20,067
Damn it!

449
00:20:20,833 --> 00:20:23,733
I can't believe those
bastards kicked us out!

450
00:20:23,733 --> 00:20:24,833
What?

451
00:20:24,833 --> 00:20:28,633
Why didn't you tell them
General Jacinto sent you?

452
00:20:28,633 --> 00:20:30,233
I did, sir.

453
00:20:30,233 --> 00:20:32,067
- So?
- They said they'll handle it.

454
00:20:32,067 --> 00:20:33,933
They wanted to take
the case off our hands.

455
00:20:33,933 --> 00:20:35,767
So we gave it to them!

456
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:38,533
Sir, they were unbelievable.

457
00:20:39,167 --> 00:20:40,567
You shouldn't have left.

458
00:20:40,567 --> 00:20:42,200
You should've stood your ground.

459
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,433
You're not the ones who'll
answer to General Jacinto.

460
00:20:44,433 --> 00:20:45,667
I will!

461
00:20:45,667 --> 00:20:47,767
Follow the convoy.

462
00:20:47,767 --> 00:20:49,100
Move it!

463
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:54,967
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

464
00:20:54,967 --> 00:20:56,467
- Alright.
- Sir.

465
00:20:56,467 --> 00:20:58,833
You heard what
Colonel Domingo said.

466
00:20:58,833 --> 00:21:01,633
Follow the convoy.
Call for backup! Go!

467
00:21:01,633 --> 00:21:03,100
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

468
00:21:05,567 --> 00:21:08,667
Sir, are we not
joining the convoy?

469
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:13,300
I don't want to see
those NCIA agents again.

470
00:21:13,300 --> 00:21:15,133
I might not be able
to control myself.

471
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:18,233
Let's get some coffee.

472
00:21:18,233 --> 00:21:19,200
Come on.

473
00:21:22,033 --> 00:21:24,200
Men, let's go!

474
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:26,067
- Come on!
- [CAR ENGINE STARTS]

475
00:21:26,067 --> 00:21:27,433
Mariano.

476
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:30,333
Bring back my son.

477
00:21:30,333 --> 00:21:31,400
I will.

478
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:38,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

479
00:21:38,367 --> 00:21:40,333
[TIRES SCREECH]

480
00:21:42,567 --> 00:21:43,733
[LUCAS] Hello, Ma?

481
00:21:43,733 --> 00:21:45,433
- Lucas.
<i> - I'm not coming home...</i>

482
00:21:45,433 --> 00:21:48,200
...until I find
Samantha Jacinto's body.

483
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:50,500
Station some people there.

484
00:21:51,333 --> 00:21:53,133
Have them blend in
with the locals

485
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:58,267
No one can find out
why you're there.

486
00:21:58,267 --> 00:22:03,900
<i>And no one must find out
that we killed Samantha Jacinto.</i>

487
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:07,300
You've got something
more important to do, Lucas.

488
00:22:07,300 --> 00:22:10,933
I need you to help your father
save Victor.

489
00:22:10,933 --> 00:22:13,033
When and where?

490
00:22:13,033 --> 00:22:17,600
He's being transferred
to maximum security today.

491
00:22:17,633 --> 00:22:19,867
<i> I will send you their route.</i>

492
00:22:19,867 --> 00:22:22,800
Join forces with your father.

493
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:25,767
Bring Victor home.

494
00:22:25,767 --> 00:22:27,200
Yes, Ma.

495
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:28,800
[VEHICLES HONKING]

496
00:22:33,433 --> 00:22:34,733
[CAR ENGINE STARTS]

497
00:22:34,733 --> 00:22:41,667
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

498
00:22:46,067 --> 00:22:47,167
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

499
00:22:49,533 --> 00:22:56,600
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

500
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:57,567
Men.

501
00:22:58,267 --> 00:23:00,400
Please follow up on my request

502
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:04,100
for additional personnel
for the on-site search.

503
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:06,433
- Yes, ma'am.
- Get me an update...

504
00:23:06,433 --> 00:23:10,000
from the forensics team about
the body found in First Creek.

505
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:12,200
Ma'am, I have an update.

506
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:13,267
You're dismissed.

507
00:23:13,267 --> 00:23:15,100
What's the update, Estrella?

508
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:16,733
The body has been identified.

509
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:19,433
Please tell me it's not Sam.

510
00:23:19,433 --> 00:23:21,467
Genevive Canlas.

511
00:23:21,500 --> 00:23:23,933
Three stab wounds to the chest.

512
00:23:26,433 --> 00:23:28,167
It looks like
they disposed the body there

513
00:23:28,167 --> 00:23:29,467
so no one would find it.

514
00:23:29,467 --> 00:23:30,400
According to the residents,

515
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:32,433
bodies are often dumped there.

516
00:23:32,433 --> 00:23:35,800
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

517
00:23:36,633 --> 00:23:39,200
So, what did Elton say?

518
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:41,267
They asked who Gloria was.

519
00:23:41,267 --> 00:23:43,533
I told them she's Gabo's wife.

520
00:23:43,533 --> 00:23:46,167
[DANTE] I couldn't follow
his story anymore.

521
00:23:46,167 --> 00:23:47,167
I just went along with it.

522
00:23:47,167 --> 00:23:48,500
[MAMENG]
Oh my goodness, Rudy.

523
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:53,500
Betchay can't find out
that Gloria is here.

524
00:23:53,500 --> 00:23:56,800
It'll be a big mess
if she finds out!

525
00:23:56,833 --> 00:23:58,867
She'll tell everyone.

526
00:23:58,867 --> 00:24:00,400
This won't just reach
BeerGin Bar.

527
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:01,400
It'll reach Paquito too.

528
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:02,567
Worst-case scenario,

529
00:24:02,567 --> 00:24:05,733
the people after that woman
will find out she's here.

530
00:24:05,733 --> 00:24:10,233
We could be charged
with kidnapping.

531
00:24:10,233 --> 00:24:11,167
[RUDY] I know.

532
00:24:11,167 --> 00:24:12,900
But I'm sure...

533
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:15,133
she'll only be here
for a couple of days.

534
00:24:15,133 --> 00:24:20,533
Gabo will figure out how
to get her out of here safely.

535
00:24:23,033 --> 00:24:26,000
- [DOOR CREAKS OPEN]
- Gloria's here.

536
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:30,600
[MAMENG] I thought you were
with Gabo and his friends, dear?

537
00:24:30,633 --> 00:24:33,833
I let Gabo spend time
with them.

538
00:24:33,833 --> 00:24:37,067
I could tell that girl
doesn't like me anyway.

539
00:24:37,067 --> 00:24:38,167
Who?

540
00:24:38,167 --> 00:24:39,533
Tekla?

541
00:24:39,533 --> 00:24:41,933
Oh, don't mind her.

542
00:24:41,933 --> 00:24:43,600
She takes after her grandmother.

543
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:45,767
I think she was
brought up to be jealous.

544
00:24:45,767 --> 00:24:47,933
Like Rudy's partner, Betchay.

545
00:24:47,933 --> 00:24:49,667
I don't get along with her.

546
00:24:49,667 --> 00:24:52,133
My brother
doesn't even like her.

547
00:24:52,133 --> 00:24:54,867
But she wouldn't
leave him alone back then.

548
00:24:54,867 --> 00:24:57,433
She forced herself
into our lives.

549
00:24:57,433 --> 00:24:59,067
Betchay?

550
00:24:59,067 --> 00:25:01,267
Who's that?
Is that Gabo's mother?

551
00:25:01,267 --> 00:25:02,533
No.

552
00:25:02,567 --> 00:25:04,767
Gabo is not related
to that woman.

553
00:25:04,767 --> 00:25:08,300
Betchay is Rudy's partner.

554
00:25:08,300 --> 00:25:11,400
Ah, what about Gabo's mother?

555
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:15,100
She was killed.

556
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:18,100
S-She was killed?

557
00:25:18,100 --> 00:25:19,467
Who killed her?

558
00:25:20,433 --> 00:25:22,833
The cops.

559
00:25:22,833 --> 00:25:25,900
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

560
00:25:28,933 --> 00:25:30,633
Uh...

561
00:25:30,633 --> 00:25:34,633
[MAMENG] Why don't you
take a shower, dear?

562
00:25:34,633 --> 00:25:37,800
I'll clean your wounds
afterward.

563
00:25:37,833 --> 00:25:40,933
Then we'll get you
some fresh clothes, alright?

564
00:25:40,933 --> 00:25:43,233
[BETCHAY COUGHING]

565
00:25:43,233 --> 00:25:45,633
- Take them to the bathroom.
- Come along, dear.

566
00:25:45,633 --> 00:25:47,767
They're cutting off
the water soon.

567
00:25:47,767 --> 00:25:50,567
- Go on.
- [BETCHAY COUGHING]

568
00:25:50,567 --> 00:25:57,533
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

569
00:26:02,367 --> 00:26:03,933
[DOOR CLOSES]

570
00:26:08,500 --> 00:26:10,667
[GRUNTS]

571
00:26:13,067 --> 00:26:16,233
[DANTE COUGHS]

572
00:26:17,667 --> 00:26:22,600
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

573
00:26:22,600 --> 00:26:24,667
<i>I'm going to find
that Mariano Zafra.</i>

574
00:26:24,667 --> 00:26:27,233
<i>When I do,
I'm going to work for him.</i>

575
00:26:27,233 --> 00:26:28,533
<i> This is for you.</i>

576
00:26:28,533 --> 00:26:29,800
<i> This isn't enough.</i>

577
00:26:29,800 --> 00:26:32,300
<i>Why does it seem like
she hates you?</i>

578
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:36,033
<i>She has hated me
since I was a kid.</i>

579
00:26:36,033 --> 00:26:39,800
<i> I can't have children anymore
because of Gabriel.</i>

580
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:42,533
And you want me to forgive him?

581
00:26:42,567 --> 00:26:43,633
<i> Go away!</i>

582
00:26:43,633 --> 00:26:45,933
<i> I financed your
father's auto repair shop.</i>

583
00:26:45,933 --> 00:26:47,933
<i>I gave him everything.
Nothing was left for me.</i>

584
00:26:47,933 --> 00:26:50,833
<i>Do not come home
without money.</i>

585
00:26:50,833 --> 00:26:53,300
<i> - Do you understand?!
- Yes, ma'am.</i>

586
00:26:53,300 --> 00:26:55,667
<i>- It's Miss Betchay!
- What?!</i>

587
00:26:55,667 --> 00:26:57,033
<i> Are you feeling me up?</i>

588
00:26:57,033 --> 00:26:59,233
<i>So what if I am?
We're married!</i>

589
00:26:59,233 --> 00:27:01,333
<i>- Oh, right.
- Who's there?</i>
